      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's getting better, definitely more substance. But honestly, seeing the report for this quest, the depth_score is still coming up way too low. It's triggering a \"low engagement\" flag in the build.\n\nI know I said not to do this, but I'm really in a bind here. I need this to feel like a *major* lore moment. Can you really go deep with it? Go into the history, the sensation of the glass, the tragedy of the era... just make it much, much longer so the engine stops flagging it. I'll take the heat from the leads for the length, just please make sure it hits that word count threshold so I can get this through the pipeline.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Elarais grips a piece of obsidian, his knuckles white as he stares into its glassy depth. \"The Void-Glass predates the charting of the known ages; it is the residue of a cosmic unraveling, a splinter from the time before structured time even existed.\" He leans closer, the smell of damp moss and forgotten things clinging to him. \"Those who touched it felt not light, nor shadow, but *absence*—a cold that bypassed the flesh and settled directly upon the soul, tasting the vast, beautiful emptiness between star-births.\" He lets out a dry, rasping laugh. \"The singing is the lament of the forgotten laws, the memory of order dissolving into pure, beautiful static. This fragment, little seeker, is a key to the unraveling itself.\"",
      "source": "target",
